WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.986
Hi, and welcome!

2
00:00:01.986 --> 00:00:06.210
Meet Codexta, the AI assistant from Codecta.

3
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.481
Here's the problem: answers are spread across reports,

4
00:00:11.481 --> 00:00:16.200
contracts and manuals, and search only gives you a list of files.

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.161
Codexta reads them for you,

6
00:00:18.161 --> 00:00:20.920
and shows where each answer came from.

7
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.522
Sarah, in finance at Harbourline,

8
00:00:24.522 --> 00:00:27.615
asks for profit over the last two years.

9
00:00:27.615 --> 00:00:30.244
No single document has both years,

10
00:00:30.244 --> 00:00:34.574
so Codexta searches year by year, reads three documents,

11
00:00:34.574 --> 00:00:37.590
and gives her one answer, with sources.

12
00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.910
Then a chart, in one sentence.

13
00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.596
Next she asks: do we work with Codecta, the software company?

14
00:00:45.596 --> 00:00:47.572
No document mentions both.

15
00:00:47.572 --> 00:00:52.056
Codexta follows the supplier contracts, one step at a time,

16
00:00:52.056 --> 00:00:53.880
and shows her the chain.

17
00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.535
Lena works in a bank's back office.

18
00:00:57.535 --> 00:01:02.372
A customer's father has died, something she handles twice a year.

19
00:01:02.372 --> 00:01:06.614
Codexta gives her the current steps from three documents,

20
00:01:06.614 --> 00:01:10.260
including last month's rule change, with sources.

21
00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.113
Support teams have a similar problem.

22
00:01:14.113 --> 00:01:16.613
A fix stays in one person's head,

23
00:01:16.613 --> 00:01:19.416
so every customer waits for a ticket.

24
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:21.840
Here's how Codexta changes that.

25
00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.348
Tom can't pay with PayPal.

26
00:01:25.348 --> 00:01:30.018
Codexta checks the knowledge base and offers an old outage,

27
00:01:30.018 --> 00:01:31.443
but that isn't it.

28
00:01:31.443 --> 00:01:33.422
So Tom asks for a person,

29
00:01:33.422 --> 00:01:36.825
and Priya from support joins the same chat.

30
00:01:36.825 --> 00:01:40.150
He doesn't have to explain anything twice.

31
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:46.502
Priya works in Codexta's support console: every chat and ticket in one place,

32
00:01:46.502 --> 00:01:48.086
the whole conversation,

33
00:01:48.086 --> 00:01:51.460
and one click to escalate a case to a specialist.

34
00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:56.079
She finds the cause: Safari's pop-up blocker.

35
00:01:56.079 --> 00:01:59.728
Priya is allowed to update the knowledge base,

36
00:01:59.728 --> 00:02:04.011
so Codexta writes a short note, without Tom's details,

37
00:02:04.011 --> 00:02:06.470
and saves it once she approves.

38
00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.652
A week later, Lukas has the same problem,

39
00:02:10.652 --> 00:02:12.486
and he writes in German.

40
00:02:12.486 --> 00:02:16.535
Codexta finds Priya's note and answers him in German.

41
00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.750
Sorted in seconds, no ticket.

42
00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.468
Already have a helpdesk?

43
00:02:21.468 --> 00:02:26.958
An admin describes it in the authoring tool and attaches the API documentation.

44
00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:31.058
Codexta builds the connection, tests it, and once approved,

45
00:02:31.058 --> 00:02:33.908
cases open where your team already works.

46
00:02:33.908 --> 00:02:36.340
Order systems connect the same way.

47
00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.721
Codexta, by Codecta.

48
00:02:38.721 --> 00:02:40.386
Bring your own documents,

49
00:02:40.386 --> 00:02:43.049
and we'll show it working in four weeks.

50
00:02:43.049 --> 00:02:44.380
Thanks for watching!

